{{also|nott|nött|Notts|Nótt}}

==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/nouht/|lang=is}} ({{audio|is-nótt.ogg|listen}})
*: {{rhymes|ouht|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|nǫ́tt|lang=non}}, {{term|nótt|lang=non}}, {{term|nátt|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|nahts|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|nókʷts|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Latin {{term|nox|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|nætur|nætur}}

# [[night]]
#: ''Ég vakti fram á '''nótt'''.''
#:: I stayed awake until late at '''night'''.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-nótt|u=u}}
The original stem is ''nátt-'' (<*''naht-''), preserved in the genitive plural (although the forms ''nótta'', ''nóttanna'' now also exist) and in all stem compounds (e.g. {{term|nátthrafn}}). The ''-ó-'' comes from earlier ''-ǫ́-'', created by u-mutation of ''-á-'', a vowel change that is no longer productive.

